hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"408","Malik ibn 'Abd al-Wahid al-Misma'i narrated to us, Rawh and Wahb narrated to us, both saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us: I heard 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb (say): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the woman to mourn her husband until her waiting period ends, seven days over her father, and three days over any besides them."
"409","Mahmud ibn Khalid and 'Amr ibn 'Uthman narrated to us, both saying: al-Walid narrated to us, from Ibn Jabir, from Makhul, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Attend your dying ones, question them, for they see, and prompt them with La ilaha illa Allah."
"410","'Abd al-Hamid ibn Bakkar al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Isma'il informed me, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Yahya ibn Jabir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what nullifies the reward for a calamity? He said: ""That a man clap his right hand upon his left."" And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clapped his right hand upon his left."
"411","Qutaybah narrated to us, Yahya — meaning Ibn Sulaym — narrated to us, from 'Imran al-Qasir, he said: The lamp of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, so he said: ""Inna lillahi wa inna ilayhi raji'un."" 'A'ishah said: This is but a lamp. He said: ""Everything that displeases the believer is a calamity."
"412","Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Salamah al-Makhzumi, he said: When news of the deaths of Ja'far and Zayd arrived, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of Zayd. When he was at the door, a daughter of Zayd met him bursting into weeping before him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wept until he sobbed. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what is this? He said: ""The longing of a beloved for a beloved."
